# Allowlist: the images are built from backend/ (both) and ui/ (the hub's
# node stage) and nothing else. A new root-level file stays out of the context
# without anyone having to remember this list. BuildKit reads the `-f`
# Containerfile outside these rules.
*
!backend
!ui

# node_modules is hundreds of megabytes that the node stage reinstalls from the
# lockfile anyway.
ui/node_modules/

# The node stage always produces dist/. A local `make fe-build` leaves hashed
# index-*.js chunks here, and COPY backend/ would carry them into the image,
# where the stage's output merges on top instead of replacing them -- so stale
# chunks shipped inside go:embed. Excluded, the image holds only what the
# stage built.
backend/internal/hub/web/dist/
